Z||000004||Eric||07-16-99||07:01 PM||||I bought a faux carbon fiber dash kit from Autotrim.  It costs about $180 and includes everything the fiero store has except the glove box area back panel.  I was impressed with the quality.  And it really dressed up the interior (very important to have the inside look as good as the outside, in case you were to get any female visitors).  If anyone is still interested, I'll get all the ordering info.<p>It may be a good idea to have someone who knows what they are doing install these kits.  If you don't line it up correctly, there is no fixing it.  I missed my mark, but I did, however, use my dremel to fudge it a little (buzz buzz).
Z||000005||Pretender||07-17-99||04:05 AM||||i've seen carbon fiber film that sticks to the plastic pieces., since our stuff is mostly flat except for around the ashtrays i wound think it rather easy to install it...it costs about $40 american from any aftermarket retailer..if i have the time a the few bucks left over i'll buy some and see how it goes from there.
Z||000006||GREENDANO||07-17-99||07:06 AM||||Check here----&gt;http://members.xoom.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm<p>I ordered a carbon fiber kit last week from Dennis. It should be here maybe today.  I'll let everyone know.<br>  Dan-O
Z||000007||GREENDANO||07-17-99||08:43 AM||||I got the kit in the mail today.  WOW!!!! This kit is the same kit that all the other Fiero stores have only better.  It also has the insert for the shift indicator on the auto console and also the insert fot the aftermarket glovebox.   The whole kit cost $95 with shipping.<br>  I talked with Dennis a week ago and he said he only had three carbon fiber kits left.  He also has woodgrain kits too.  I would suggest that if you're interested in a carbon fiber kit you call or order it ASAP.  It's a great deal!<br>  I'm installing it this afternoon, gona be 95 degrees this afternoon so I'm sure it will stick.  That, of course, is dependant on how many trips to the beer cooler I take between panels.  :)<br>  Dan-O
